## Nodes

A node in a k8s is a machine or server where an application is running.

### Master Node or Control Plane Node

K8s' brain where makes decision such as where to load app, how many copies to run, and what to do when something crashes.

### Worker Node

It is a place where an application runs. It follows commands from the Control plane.

#### Sidecars / helper containers

Implementing infrastructure related changes to code-base raises serveral issues, like:

- Repeat the same logging logic across all services, including Auth-service, User-service, Order-service, and Payment-service, would increase LOE.
- A Bug in logging code can crash the main application.
- Updating to logger requires re-deploying the main app.
- Tight-coupling to the logger. Moving to different logger requires great LOE.

Instead of writing logging code, we could create container and attaches it to every services. This would create lossly coupling.
